# localhost works from the iOS Simulator (shares the Mac's network stack) and
# when running the app on web. Testing on a physical device via Expo Go needs
# your machine's LAN IP instead — "localhost" there means the phone itself.
#
# If you switch to the LAN IP, also update
# services/collections-service/src/CollectionsService.Api/appsettings.Development.json
# (Keycloak:Authority) to the SAME host. Keycloak (start-dev, no KC_HOSTNAME set)
# puts whatever hostname was used to reach it into the token's issuer — if
# collections-service validates against a different host than the one that
# issued the token, JWT validation fails with an issuer mismatch.
EXPO_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=http://localhost:8080/realms/project
EXPO_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=mobile-app
EXPO_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:5096
